  "name": "rust-dotenv",
  "description": "A specialized Rust implementation for managing configuration via environment variables through .env file parsing. It mimics the standard library's environment API to provide a seamless drop-in replacement for development and testing contexts, merging file-based variables with system-level environment state. The implementation utilizes regular expressions for robust line-based parsing and handles byte-level data to ensure compatibility with diverse character encodings.",
